      "label": "Title: Ancient Egypt: The Pyramids",
      "type": "text",
      "duration": 3.0,
      "content_summary": "Lesson title"
    },
    {
      "id": "CK12-HIST-003-U002",
      "label": "Purpose of the pyramids (text)",
      "type": "text",
      "duration": 30.0,
      "content_summary": "Egyptian pyramids were built as tombs for pharaohs, believed to help the king's soul ascend to the afterlife. The Great Pyramid of Giza, built for Pharaoh Khufu around 2560 BCE, is the largest and best preserved."
    },
    {
      "id": "CK12-HIST-003-U003",
      "label": "Great Pyramid photo (image)",
      "type": "image",
      "duration": 15.0,
      "content_summary": "Photograph of the Great Pyramid of Giza with the Sphinx in the foreground, showing scale relative to visitors."
    },
    {
      "id": "CK12-HIST-003-U004",
      "label": "Construction methods (text)",
      "type": "text",
      "duration": 30.0,
      "content_summary": "Built using over 2 million limestone blocks, some weighing several tons. Historians debate the exact methods (ramps, levers, sledges) but agree it required immense organized labor, estimated tens of thousands of workers over roughly 20 years."
    },
    {
      "id": "CK12-HIST-003-U005",
      "label": "Cross-section diagram (image)",
      "type": "image",
      "duration": 15.0,
      "content_summary": "Cross-section diagram of the Great Pyramid showing internal chambers: the King's Chamber, Queen's Chamber, and Grand Gallery, with passage angles labeled."
    },
    {
      "id": "CK12-HIST-003-U006",
      "label": "Practice questions (text)",
      "type": "text",
      "duration": 18.0,
      "content_summary": "Three questions: why were pyramids built; who was Khufu; what evidence do historians use to study pyramid construction."
    },
    {
      "id": "CK12-HIST-003-U007",
      "label": "Lesson root: Ancient Egypt Pyramids",
